check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6445308Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6454322Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6545666Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6554404Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6555055Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6555688Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6555945Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6556170Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6556791Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6557119Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6557351Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6558414Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6558751Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6559295Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6559945Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6560855Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6561275Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6561539Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6561868Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6562170Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6562429Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6562864Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6563006Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6563227Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6563437Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6563984Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6564931Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6565737Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6566278Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6566561Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6566829Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6567419Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6567969Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6568442Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6568833Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6569228Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6569758Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6570250Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6581026Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6582063Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6592776Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6593693Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6594015Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6598658Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6599254Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6614818Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6615903Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6624524Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6625344Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6625842Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6626058Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6626261Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6626580Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6626882Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6627336Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6627573Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6627734Z If you would like to
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6628096Z see the output, try like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6628343Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6628573Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6629155Z   $ sh ./install-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6629349Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6629391Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:42.6629730Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
