check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4595500Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4605780Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4710144Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4720519Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4721199Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4722054Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4722956Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4723601Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4724538Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4725100Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4725426Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4725874Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4726095Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4726848Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4727501Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4728023Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4728404Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4728727Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4728932Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4729230Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4729456Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4729876Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4730027Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4730144Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4730320Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4730614Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4731129Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4733702Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4733924Z I will:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4734272Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4734641Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4735265Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4735732Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4736158Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4736477Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4736783Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4737233Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4737668Z    /root
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4750264Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4751027Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4762397Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4763956Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4764504Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4764989Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:04:41.4765687Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
